1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,640
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,360
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,680
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,160
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,239
Krisdanai Rome Lee,

6
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,880
you must prepare yourself
to become ARSENI’s next leader.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,640
Must be nice being an heir
to the Lee family.

8
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,000
You get to decide for yourself.

9
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,280
Lookpeach’s not the only one I care about.

10
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:25,320
I care about you too, Rome.

11
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,120
I guess I’ll have to give you
your secretary back.

12
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:30,160
I know you can handle it all
at the same time, P’Kian.

13
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:32,200
I did this for Mr. Thee.

14
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,280
You wrote a song, Peach?

15
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,440
I wanted to give something back
for all the love you’ve given me.

16
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,480
But what else could I do?

17
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,680
I can’t sing.

18
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,680
It’s our post-wedding dinner.

19
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,200
Of course it can’t be ordinary.

20
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:05,280
Which one is the Peachayarat Star
that we bought?

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,080
That one?

22
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:09,360
Or that one?

23
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,680
Or…

24
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:13,480
This one?

25
00:01:18,039 --> 00:01:22,080
Didn’t they tell you
it’s just a naming service?

26
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,280
You don’t actually own a star.

27
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:35,840
Mira.

28
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,039
(Yes, Mr. Thee.)

29
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,479
Get NASA on the line.

30
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:40,479
(Excuse me?)

31
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:43,080
Tell them we’re renaming a planet.

32
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,160
Any planet.

33
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:47,280
Mercury, Venus,

34
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:51,280
Earth, Mars, Jupiter,

35
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:54,000
Saturn, Uranus, Neptune.

36
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:57,880
Whichever one’s easiest to see.

37
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:01,800
Ms. Mira, you can call it a night.

38
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,440
Everything Mr. Thee just ordered,

39
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,680
you can forget it.

40
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,560
Good night.

41
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,880
(Thank you, Mr. Peach.)

42
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,800
Don’t think I can’t do it, Lookpeach.

43
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,280
It’s because I know you can.

44
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:20,560
A man like you can do anything.

45
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,200
I wanted to surprise you,

46
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,320
but I ended up being the one surprised.

47
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,280
I heard it was our post-wedding dinner,

48
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,520
so I wanted to make it extra special.

49
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:49,000
Now…

50
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:54,360
sing into my ear
the song you wrote for me.

51
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,400
No.

52
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,280
I don’t sing well.

53
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,280
Hmm…

54
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:04,560
You do.

55
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,280
I do?

56
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:14,440
Not just your singing.

57
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,040
Even the sound of your breathing

58
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,600
is music to my heart.

59
00:03:23,079 --> 00:03:23,880
P’Kian.

60
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,280
Please, baby.

61
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:32,079
Sing for me.

62
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:45,680
♪ You’re my only focus ♪

63
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,040
Melodious!

64
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,200
It totally touched my heart.

65
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,079
That’s not where your heart is.

66
00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:00,560
I…

67
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,320
like red.

68
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:18,960
Taking a walk?

69
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:21,880
Ms. Panachakorn.

70
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,080
It’s late. What are you doing out here?

71
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,800
I left this in my car.

72
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,920
I was worried these little ones
couldn’t breathe.

73
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:31,880
If you’re done,

74
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:34,080
you should get some rest, Ms. Lookplub.

75
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,880
It’s late. It’s not safe.

76
00:05:37,159 --> 00:05:38,960
But Thee said it’s safe here.

77
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:41,960
Even so, you’re a woman.

78
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,920
You shouldn’t be out here alone this late.

79
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,880
You’re out here alone too, Mira.

80
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,080
Are you on patrol?

81
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,640
Need a tour guide?

82
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,680
I know every corner of this place.

83
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:58,880
ARSENI’s bodyguards
aren’t just responsible for security.

84
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,480
We’re expected to know everything
about our bosses,

85
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,560
including the layout of the estate.

86
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:06,160
A place this important,

87
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,560
I must know it well enough
to walk through it with my eyes closed.

88
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,680
I want to put these flowers in a vase
in the glasshouse.

89
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,200
Close your eyes and take me there.

90
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:22,680
Let’s go.

91
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,000
Very well.

92
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:25,600
This way, please.

93
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,400
Are you sure?

94
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,680
Watch your step.

95
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,680
There’s one step here.

96
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:42,400
We’ve arrived.

97
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:49,200
You really can find your way
with your eyes closed.

98
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,159
Impressive.

99
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,480
It’s getting really late.

100
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,080
You should arrange your flowers
and get some sleep, Ms. Panachakorn.

101
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:03,160
Do you have a nickname, Mira?

102
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:06,160
No, ma’am.

103
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:10,360
Well, I do.

104
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,440
You can call me Plub.

105
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:14,600
I know.

106
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,080
Then please do.

107
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:22,200
Thee told me
you’re going to be his secretary.

108
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,880
But you just said
you’re an ARSENI bodyguard.

109
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:28,480
So, that means…

110
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,280
you do both, like Mr. Mok?

111
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,760
Something like that, ma’am.

112
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,880
So you’re one of Dad’s people,

113
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,800
sent here from Hong Kong?

114
00:07:41,159 --> 00:07:43,000
You’re Thai.

115
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,800
Where’s your family?

116
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,200
Here or in Hong Kong?

117
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,360
Why do you ask?

118
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,560
Well, if your family’s in Thailand,

119
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:57,360
then being transferred here must be nice.

120
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,960
You get to come home.

121
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,560
But if they’re in Hong Kong,

122
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,880
that’s not so great

123
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,600
because you have to be apart from them.

124
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,160
I don’t have any family.

125
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,840
Not here.

126
00:08:20,480 --> 00:08:21,400
Not there.

127
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:29,360
ARSENI’s bodyguards are chosen
from people with no families,

128
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:32,120
no one depending on them.

129
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:37,080
The Lee family didn’t just give us jobs.

130
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:41,360
They gave us new lives and an education,

131
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,280
in exchange for our loyalty.

132
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:51,680
But those lives still
belong to the Lee family.

133
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,280
Then you’re lucky, Mira,

134
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,000
that you get to work for Thee.

135
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,360
Because it’s safe here.

136
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:09,160
You seem to say that word a lot.

137
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:10,480
I do.

138
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,080
Because Thee doesn’t just say it.

139
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:14,960
He shows it.

140
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:21,040
He also became a family to Peach and me.

141
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,680
Family?

142
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:36,160
If ARSENI’s bodyguards really
know everything about their bosses,

143
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:42,880
then you should know
Peach and I are orphans too.

144
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,760
Another nightmare?

145
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,080
My baby.

146
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:15,280
I’m sorry I woke you, P’Kian.

147
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,000
Don’t.

148
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,160
Go back to sleep.

149
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,880
I’m okay.

150
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:50,280
(There’s something
I’ve never planned to tell you.)

151
00:10:53,080 --> 00:10:54,680
(It’s not that I’m trying to hide it.)

152
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:57,360
(I just don’t know what good it would do…)

153
00:10:58,280 --> 00:11:02,640
if you and Lookplub learned about it.

154
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,600
It has something to do with Lookplub too?

155
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:20,160
Why do you want to give
all these to Mother?

156
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,080
Mother said there are
lots of new children in the foster home.

157
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:27,000
So Marn and I want to give them our toys.

158
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:34,680
You hug this doll to sleep every night.

159
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:35,960
Don’t you like it anymore?

160
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:37,600
Because I like it so much,

161
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:40,760
I think the children there
will like it too.

162
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,680
Doesn’t it make you sad,

163
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,480
giving away your favorite thing?

164
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:54,760
I have Dad, Peach, you, Mork,
Uncle Rome, and everyone else here.

165
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:58,640
Even if I gave away all my dolls,
I still wouldn’t feel lonely.

166
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,280
Oh, I’ve been meaning to ask.

167
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,600
How’s life here?

168
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,280
Any problems?

169
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,040
None at all.

170
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:14,400
Everyone here loves Mork and me.

171
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:16,960
That’s good.

172
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:19,760
You two are luckier than most children,

173
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:22,480
and luckier than Peach and I ever were.

174
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,560
You’ve been given a wonderful opportunity,
so be good kids.

175
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,000
Behave yourselves.

176
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,880
Make everyone proud, especially Dad.

177
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:30,560
Understand?

178
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,360
Good.

179
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,880
Lookplub has grown up so much.

180
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:54,880
About that, I think it’s time she knew.

181
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:58,080
What she chooses to do with it,

182
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,680
that’s up to her.

183
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:05,080
Hey, Thee. Peach.

184
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:07,280
Why are you two just standing there?

185
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,800
Catch up with Mork.

186
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,160
Careful.

187
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:20,280
Lookplub, when are you
going back to your place?

188
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:22,200
Monday, I think.

189
00:13:22,560 --> 00:13:25,800
I’ll go to work with Thee,
then head to my place after work.

190
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:28,160
Why do you ask?

191
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,120
Yes?

192
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:59,920
DEATH CERTIFICATE

193
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:04,400
After I asked Mok
to look into your background,

194
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:09,760
the only record he found
was your younger sister’s.

195
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,880
But not long after,

196
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,760
he brought me this additional document.

197
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,360
Why are you telling me now?

198
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:23,000
If running away over ten years ago
still gives you nightmares,

199
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:26,480
maybe…

200
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:30,840
it’s better if you face it.

201
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,680
Face it?

202
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:38,000
I’m not asking you to forgive anyone.

203
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,360
I just want you to know
that the people who haunt your nightmares

204
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,120
can never hurt you or your sister again.

205
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,480
Mom…

206
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,160
died many years ago.

207
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,680
Did that man do it?

208
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,080
No.

209
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:14,200
He was sentenced to life in prison.

210
00:15:15,760 --> 00:15:17,360
He lost his freedom

211
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:21,920
not long after you and your sister
ended up at Baan Klamai.

212
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,280
And…

213
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,200
your mother was ill.

214
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,200
She wasn’t assaulted.

215
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,600
I barely have any memories of her.

216
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,200
Maybe I was too young

217
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:49,080
or maybe I just chose to forget.

218
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:55,400
At first, I wasn’t sure
if I should tell you

219
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,960
or just let these people…

220
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,440
disappear from our lives.

221
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:12,000
So why did you decide to tell me?

222
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:19,680
Because I think we’ve both…
walked far enough away from it.

223
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,880
Far enough to face it

224
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,560
and leave those nightmares behind.

225
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,120
Tomorrow, I’m taking Lookpeach
to visit her.

226
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:41,520
Would you like to come too, Lookplub?

227
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:58,200
If you don’t want to go,

228
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:01,080
don’t feel bad.

229
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:04,079
Whatever you decide,

230
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,280
I’m okay with it.

231
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,160
You know that, right?

232
00:17:13,359 --> 00:17:16,160
I’m just surprised by how I feel.

233
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,599
How you feel?

234
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:32,280
Can you explain to me how you feel?

235
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,800
I feel nothing at all.

236
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,760
I’m not sad

237
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,560
but I’m not happy either.

238
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:50,080
A person died.

239
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:56,000
So why don’t I feel anything?

240
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,000
Don’t be surprised.

241
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:05,080
I’m just like you.

242
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,520
P’Kian said

243
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,920
maybe it’s because
we never bonded with her.

244
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,040
That’s why we’re not sad.

245
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,400
But if you never bonded with her,

246
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:22,880
why do you want to visit her?

247
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,600
(She never showed me any love,)

248
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,680
but she never treated me
with hatred either.

249
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,000
She never hit me,

250
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:35,760
but she never protected me either.

251
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:41,000
That’s all I remember about my mom.

252
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:46,240
As for the good memories…

253
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,080
I can’t think of a single one.

254
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:58,880
Then let this be
the one good memory you have of her.

255
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,640
When you can’t help thinking of her,

256
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:08,600
let this memory replace
all the painful ones.

257
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,080
So neither of you owes the other anything.

258
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:19,000
I want to thank her myself.

259
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:29,920
After all, she gave me
the most precious person in my life,

260
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,680
whether she meant to or not.

261
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,160
I want to thank her…

262
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:42,360
for bringing you into this world,
Lookpeach.

263
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,480
She also…

264
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:10,960
gave me the most precious person
in my life.

265
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,440
Don’t be afraid.

266
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:16,080
I’ll protect you, Lookplub.

267
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,320
I’ll stay with you, Peach.

268
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:27,480
I’m so glad…

269
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:31,600
Thee exists.

270
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,400
Otherwise, I can’t imagine anyone else

271
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,120
who could take care of someone

272
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:41,080
who’s always taken
such good care of himself, like you.

273
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:47,600
You two really were made for each other.

274
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,160
Maybe…

275
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,640
he really was born for me.

276
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:05,680
Well, well.

277
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,880
Ever since you two fell head over heels,

278
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:12,000
you don’t leave the rest of us
any room to tease you.

279
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:14,720
I just sit back and watch you two
swoon over each other.

280
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,880
That’s because I’ve never loved
anyone this much before.

281
00:21:19,360 --> 00:21:19,960
Peach!

282
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,600
Do you realize what you just said?

283
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:22,800
Of course.

284
00:21:23,720 --> 00:21:25,480
You think that just slipped out?

285
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:27,760
I really love him.

286
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:28,680
Stop.

287
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,840
You’re making me blush.

288
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:33,240
When I keep it to myself,
you say I’m too reserved.

289
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,880
When I tell you how I really feel,
you can’t handle it.

290
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,080
Lookplub,

291
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:50,360
do you know how much I love you?

292
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:52,800
I do.

293
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:56,800
How does Thee do it, though?

294
00:21:58,080 --> 00:22:02,000
Not only did he never
take your love away from me like I feared…

295
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,400
he somehow made us
love each other even more.

296
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:11,240
The green flag we all dream of.

297
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:18,640
LIBERATION SANCTUARY

298
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:44,760
PANIDA YAMSAWAN
11 SEP 1976 - 31 DEC 2012

299
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:53,440
The restaurant said they’ve reserved
the whole salmon just for you, sir.

300
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:56,080
Any special requests, Mr. Thee?

301
00:22:56,960 --> 00:22:57,760
No need.

302
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:03,760
An ordinary life
is all I need to be happy.

303
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:06,760
And you…

304
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:11,000
How much longer are you planning
to keep this cold war going?

305
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:11,600
Pardon?

306
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,560
Keeping your distance
to “sort out your feelings”?

307
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
You think you’re starring in a soap opera?

308
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,480
This is real life, bro.

309
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:21,480
Keep playing hard to get,

310
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,760
and you’ll be on the shelf forever.

311
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:27,880
Easy for you to say.
You’re not the one pushed away.

312
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:31,680
What if Mr. Peach’s life plan
never included you?

313
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:33,120
How would you feel?

314
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:38,120
Rome waited ten years for you, dude.

315
00:23:38,400 --> 00:23:39,160
And now,

316
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:41,640
when it’s your turn to chase him,

317
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:45,240
all you do is mope around.

318
00:23:46,360 --> 00:23:47,760
Mope around? Who’s moping?

319
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:51,240
If you’re really not meant to be together,
save it for your next life.

320
00:23:51,840 --> 00:23:53,840
As for this one, just stay friends.

321
00:23:56,040 --> 00:23:57,160
Stay friends after we already
fell for each other?

322
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:58,160
Screw you!

323
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,760
What are you looking at?

324
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:04,880
Like you’re some kind of love guru.

325
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:08,400
At least I have a marriage certificate.

326
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:11,280
Excuse me. I…

327
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:12,280
No.

328
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:13,200
Stay here.

329
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:14,480
Don’t let him out of sight.

330
00:24:14,640 --> 00:24:16,640
And if you could shut him up,
I’d appreciate it.

331
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:20,200
Call him once in a while.

332
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,480
Swallow your pride.

333
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:24,640
At least you’ll get to hear his voice.

334
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:31,200
Hopelessly slow.

335
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:33,960
Three steps forward, four steps back.

336
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:37,280
Boss, are you talking to me?

337
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:39,680
One day, they’ll be hugging
their knees in tears.

338
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,240
Nope, not freakin’ talking to me.

339
00:24:48,080 --> 00:24:52,200
Uh, if you don’t need anything else,
I’ll go check on those two.

340
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,440
No matter who we are,

341
00:24:54,120 --> 00:24:56,280
love brings us all to our knees.

342
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:00,760
The human heart…

343
00:25:01,320 --> 00:25:02,600
is beyond anyone’s understanding.

344
00:25:11,640 --> 00:25:13,440
We don’t owe each other anything anymore.

345
00:25:15,760 --> 00:25:17,400
I’m not angry with you anymore.

346
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:21,600
I hope you’ve gone to a better place.

347
00:25:23,120 --> 00:25:24,560
And if there’s a next life,

348
00:25:26,560 --> 00:25:28,560
I hope you have a loving family.

349
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:56,040
THEEPEACH 1
BANGKOK

350
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:08,880
STOP SULKING, BUD.

351
00:26:10,960 --> 00:26:12,840
(RO) M ♥

352
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:42,160
I’ll cover you.

353
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:43,320
Can you make it to the car in ten seconds?

354
00:26:43,360 --> 00:26:44,080
I only need five.

355
00:26:44,320 --> 00:26:45,560
But I’m not going to the car.

356
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:49,880
Mr. Peach!

357
00:27:04,480 --> 00:27:06,880
Shooting is a sport
for people who can stay calm.

358
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:10,400
I’m teaching you to see it as a sport,
not a way to take lives.

359
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,360
Where’s the boss?

360
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:21,480
Mr. Thee.

361
00:27:21,520 --> 00:27:22,480
I asked, where’s the boss?

362
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:23,680
Mr. Mok, go help P’Kian.

363
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,160
We’ve got this.

364
00:27:32,120 --> 00:27:32,960
What do you want?

365
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,760
What do you want from us?

366
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:36,880
Get him.

367
00:27:51,680 --> 00:27:52,360
Mr. Thee!

368
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:55,960
Mok!

369
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,360
Don’t kill him, Rome.

370
00:28:40,840 --> 00:28:42,000
SANCTUARY

371
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:44,320
PLEASE REFRAIN FROM HARMING
OR TAKING ANY LIFE.

372
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:50,760
Are you sure?

373
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,760
I’m really okay.

374
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:57,760
The doctor said everything’s normal.

375
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:00,960
I was just in shock earlier.

376
00:29:07,560 --> 00:29:08,840
It’s over now.

377
00:29:09,600 --> 00:29:14,080
I won’t let anything like that
happen again.

378
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:22,720
Yes.

379
00:29:24,440 --> 00:29:26,120
But take care of yourself too.

380
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:29,080
And…

381
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:35,960
there’s someone who’s probably
worried so much about you right now.

382
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:53,080
Are you blaming yourself?

383
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:07,760
Do you feel guilty
for putting everyone in danger?

384
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:09,960
For Mr. Mok getting hurt?

385
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:14,080
For bringing Lookplub to the hospital?

386
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:16,240
Lookpeach.

387
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:18,760
Is any of that really your fault, P’Kian?

388
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:26,560
I wanted to take you there
so you could finally find some peace.

389
00:30:29,080 --> 00:30:31,080
Instead, I only gave you
one more thing to worry about.

390
00:30:48,240 --> 00:30:49,480
How’s your little sister?

391
00:30:50,360 --> 00:30:51,840
There’s nothing to worry about.

392
00:30:57,520 --> 00:30:59,480
Lookplub will never trust me again.

393
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:01,160
She doesn’t feel that way.

394
00:31:02,720 --> 00:31:04,320
She knows you meant well.

395
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:08,760
And she cares about you
every bit as much as I do.

396
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:16,280
Don’t get so busy caring
for everyone else…

397
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:19,960
that you forget you’re cared for too.

398
00:32:07,160 --> 00:32:08,640
They were low-ranking ARSENI members.

399
00:32:09,560 --> 00:32:11,520
They wanted to seize the power
I’m about to inherit.

400
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:15,680
Their bodies had been sent back.

401
00:32:17,480 --> 00:32:20,480
That should keep them quiet
for quite a while.

402
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:24,760
I’m sorry, Peach, if I scared you.

403
00:32:26,840 --> 00:32:29,360
You guys weren’t their target.

404
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:34,760
I was.

405
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:37,360
I’m all right.

406
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:44,440
Once I officially take over from Dad,

407
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:48,120
I’ll have more control.

408
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:52,560
-What happened at the cemetery…
-Why did you have to kill them?

409
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,840
The ARSENI under my watch,

410
00:32:58,360 --> 00:32:59,320
no one has to die.

411
00:32:59,320 --> 00:33:00,480
If I hadn’t killed them,

412
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:03,560
the one lying dead

413
00:33:04,880 --> 00:33:06,080
could’ve been you…

414
00:33:07,040 --> 00:33:07,480
or Mok.

415
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:08,480
There had to be another way.

416
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:09,480
There wasn’t.

417
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,680
I won’t stand by
and watch Mok get hurt like that again.

418
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:15,480
Do you understand?

419
00:33:19,480 --> 00:33:22,760
Don’t ever do this again in my territory.

420
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:24,960
Fine. I’ll leave as soon as I can.

421
00:33:27,040 --> 00:33:29,680
So your territory won’t be
thrown into chaos…

422
00:33:31,480 --> 00:33:32,480
because of me.

423
00:33:48,480 --> 00:33:50,600
Move me to the earliest survival flight.

424
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:02,520
Hey.

425
00:34:03,840 --> 00:34:04,720
Why did you get up?

426
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:06,440
Can you wait for me?

427
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:08,960
Wait?

428
00:34:09,239 --> 00:34:10,560
Wait until I’ve fully recovered.

429
00:34:11,679 --> 00:34:12,880
Then we’ll go together.

430
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:16,960
Mok…

431
00:34:20,639 --> 00:34:21,920
The time we spent apart,

432
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:25,040
I don’t know if it was enough for you

433
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:28,040
to figure out how you feel.

434
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:33,280
But it was enough for me

435
00:34:35,560 --> 00:34:36,840
to realize…

436
00:34:39,679 --> 00:34:41,239
I can’t let you go.

437
00:34:44,760 --> 00:34:47,760
Did you really think it through
before you said it?

438
00:34:48,679 --> 00:34:51,440
I said it because
I didn’t need to think anymore.

439
00:34:58,720 --> 00:35:00,280
I couldn’t live without you either.

440
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:02,640
That’s why I came back.

441
00:35:05,840 --> 00:35:06,400
Ow!

442
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,640
Oh.

443
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,040
Sorry.

444
00:35:09,600 --> 00:35:10,960
I forgot. Does it hurt?

445
00:35:15,120 --> 00:35:15,960
No.

446
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:18,680
Not as much as when you told me to leave.

447
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:22,440
I didn’t mean to say that.

448
00:35:23,680 --> 00:35:24,680
Sorry.

449
00:35:26,560 --> 00:35:27,360
Okay?

450
00:35:36,680 --> 00:35:39,160
Who promised me
he wouldn’t get hurt again?

451
00:35:44,520 --> 00:35:45,960
You want to punish me?

452
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:49,160
I’m all yours.

453
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:51,360
Does it hurt anywhere else?

454
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,800
Are you sure it doesn’t hurt right here?

455
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:08,760
I made you a promise.

456
00:36:11,640 --> 00:36:14,080
Under my protection, you’d be safe.

457
00:36:18,920 --> 00:36:20,760
This should never have happened.

458
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:26,920
I remember every promise you made me.

459
00:36:28,520 --> 00:36:32,960
And I know how hard you tried
to keep them.

460
00:36:35,080 --> 00:36:36,360
Sometimes,

461
00:36:37,880 --> 00:36:39,960
trying your best to keep a promise

462
00:36:40,960 --> 00:36:42,920
matters more than actually keeping it.

463
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,480
I’m okay.

464
00:36:51,120 --> 00:36:52,960
I got to use everything you taught me.

465
00:36:54,240 --> 00:36:56,760
Shooting and martial arts.

466
00:36:57,400 --> 00:36:58,800
It’s a shame you weren’t there to see it.

467
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:00,680
Even Lookplub said I was so cool today—

468
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:09,440
Thank you for being strong

469
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:12,880
when I am at my weakest.

470
00:37:24,560 --> 00:37:26,160
Well, we’re life partners.

471
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:30,960
Whenever your burden gets too heavy,

472
00:37:32,520 --> 00:37:33,560
set it down

473
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:36,960
and let me carry it with you.

474
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:27,280
One night in the hospital

475
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:31,040
won’t ruin your reputation
as an ARSENI bodyguard.

476
00:38:38,680 --> 00:38:39,880
I’m fine now.

477
00:38:41,440 --> 00:38:42,880
Why waste a hospital bed on me?

478
00:38:56,760 --> 00:38:58,160
Are you really coming with me?

479
00:39:04,640 --> 00:39:05,280
I am.

480
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:10,640
As what?

481
00:39:17,320 --> 00:39:18,560
That’s for you to decide.

482
00:39:20,600 --> 00:39:21,760
If it’s up to me,

483
00:39:23,280 --> 00:39:25,320
then stop trying to shoot
with your left hand.

484
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:30,280
Don’t force yourself
to become someone you’re not

485
00:39:32,240 --> 00:39:33,360
just because of me.

486
00:39:37,440 --> 00:39:38,400
You knew?

487
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:41,840
I won’t make you my bodyguard,

488
00:39:42,520 --> 00:39:43,480
my secretary,

489
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:45,440
or my assistant.

490
00:39:47,040 --> 00:39:48,280
If you’re coming,

491
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:51,880
there’s only one position available.

492
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,920
And that is my partner.

493
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:02,640
Whatever position is available,

494
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:04,640
I’ll take it.

495
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:45,080
Deal?

496
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:57,680
How am I supposed to trust you
to work on your own?

497
00:40:58,520 --> 00:40:59,680
When danger struck,

498
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:02,120
you didn’t even know where the boss was.

499
00:41:03,360 --> 00:41:04,040
I’m sorry, sir.

500
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:07,360
Let me ask you this.

501
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:08,800
Are you truly ready for this job?

502
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,960
Mr. Mok, you can’t fire Mira.

503
00:41:12,440 --> 00:41:14,160
Ms. Lookplub, please cooperate.

504
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,280
Don’t interfere with my work.

505
00:41:18,400 --> 00:41:20,760
But she was looking after Peach and me.

506
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:21,960
She wasn’t neglecting her duty.

507
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:24,680
But her duty is to protect Mr. Thee.

508
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,680
Isn’t Peach the person Thee loves most?

509
00:41:33,920 --> 00:41:37,800
Protecting Peach
means protecting Thee’s heart.

510
00:41:38,760 --> 00:41:40,360
-Ms. Lookplub…
-Please, Mr. Mok.

511
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:43,680
Just this once.

512
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:47,560
Don’t let Mira go.

513
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:58,360
Don’t let it happen again.

514
00:41:59,720 --> 00:42:00,640
Yes, sir.

515
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:10,880
You got an earful.

516
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:14,280
I deserved it.

517
00:42:15,160 --> 00:42:16,160
What about you?

518
00:42:16,480 --> 00:42:17,760
Why did you stand up for me?

519
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:19,320
You got scolded too.

520
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:24,880
You saved me yesterday.

521
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:28,080
Today, I returned the favor.

522
00:42:28,600 --> 00:42:29,680
Now we’re even.

523
00:42:33,040 --> 00:42:34,240
You’re stubborn.

524
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:43,080
That was a close one.

525
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:50,280
You’re up, Mr. Rome?

526
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:51,920
Morning, Peach.

527
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:04,680
Shouldn’t you talk to your brother?

528
00:43:05,200 --> 00:43:06,680
You shouldn’t leave things like this.

529
00:43:14,560 --> 00:43:16,320
Rome killed people without blinking.

530
00:43:18,040 --> 00:43:19,880
I’ve never seen him like that.

531
00:43:21,280 --> 00:43:22,560
And I never want to again.

532
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:24,680
P’Kian…

533
00:43:29,200 --> 00:43:31,080
He acts like people’s lives are worthless.

534
00:43:36,720 --> 00:43:37,520
Rome…

535
00:43:40,560 --> 00:43:41,560
is just like Dad.

536
00:43:44,040 --> 00:43:45,360
Look at it this way.

537
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:52,360
If it hadn’t been Mr. Mok who got shot…

538
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:55,040
but me instead,

539
00:43:56,320 --> 00:43:58,360
wouldn’t you have done
the same as Mr. Rome?

540
00:44:06,360 --> 00:44:07,040
Ouch!

541
00:44:08,280 --> 00:44:08,960
Don’t shoot.

542
00:44:09,120 --> 00:44:11,680
I’m not going to kill him,
but he needs to hurt more than you do.

543
00:44:12,560 --> 00:44:13,320
Many times more.

544
00:44:15,640 --> 00:44:17,400
Mr. Rome isn’t cruel.

545
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:20,520
He just loves Mr. Mok that much.

546
00:44:35,720 --> 00:44:39,240
(And he’s truly ready to lead ARSENI.)

547
00:44:46,400 --> 00:44:47,360
When did you get here?

548
00:44:52,960 --> 00:44:54,480
I took it out on you yesterday.

549
00:44:55,880 --> 00:44:56,760
I’m sorry.

550
00:44:58,160 --> 00:44:59,080
I didn’t mean to.

551
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:01,760
Yeah.

552
00:45:03,080 --> 00:45:04,440
I’m sorry too…

553
00:45:07,400 --> 00:45:08,760
for doing that on your turf.

554
00:45:13,480 --> 00:45:17,440
Peach told me you did it
because you love Mok so much.

555
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:20,280
Now that I think about it…

556
00:45:20,840 --> 00:45:22,480
if Peach had been in danger,

557
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:24,360
I would’ve done the same.

558
00:45:29,080 --> 00:45:31,880
The succession’s been moved up.

559
00:45:34,000 --> 00:45:38,480
So that means I’ll have to return
to Hong Kong sooner.

560
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:40,480
How soon are we talking?

561
00:45:41,360 --> 00:45:42,640
As soon as Mok recovers.

562
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:44,280
Why the rush?

563
00:45:45,040 --> 00:45:48,280
So your home can finally be peaceful.

564
00:45:48,520 --> 00:45:50,480
But this is your home too.

565
00:45:56,480 --> 00:45:59,960
Let this always be our safe haven.

566
00:46:01,360 --> 00:46:03,680
Whenever I need a break, I’ll come here.

567
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:06,680
Is that okay?

568
00:46:06,720 --> 00:46:10,360
Do you remember what you said before?

569
00:46:12,040 --> 00:46:13,240
It’s just a slight change of plans.

570
00:46:13,720 --> 00:46:14,960
Instead of being your right-hand man,

571
00:46:16,760 --> 00:46:18,280
I’ll just be the leader.

572
00:46:21,040 --> 00:46:22,800
Today, you become the leader,

573
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:26,960
and I’ll be your right-hand man.

574
00:46:30,480 --> 00:46:31,560
Don’t get sentimental.

575
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:32,960
It’s cringe.

576
00:46:33,840 --> 00:46:34,880
I’m not used to this.

577
00:46:35,560 --> 00:46:37,160
Like I go around saying things like that.

578
00:46:38,200 --> 00:46:39,360
It’s giving me goosebumps.

579
00:46:45,280 --> 00:46:46,960
These two can never
stay mad at each other for long.

580
00:46:47,640 --> 00:46:49,000
They just like pouting at each other.

581
00:46:51,680 --> 00:46:53,320
We’ve been through
something awful together.

582
00:46:54,280 --> 00:46:57,880
How about we do something fun
once the rain stops?

583
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:00,680
Sure.

584
00:47:07,280 --> 00:47:10,360
I miss the time
the three of us went camping together.

585
00:47:10,560 --> 00:47:11,280
Remember?

586
00:47:13,080 --> 00:47:14,640
You know, Peach,

587
00:47:14,640 --> 00:47:16,880
we built a campfire
and grilled food just like this.

588
00:47:17,080 --> 00:47:18,080
But you know what happened?

589
00:47:18,360 --> 00:47:20,360
There was dry grass nearby.

590
00:47:20,840 --> 00:47:23,800
Our tent was on fire.
The whole campsite caught fire.

591
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:24,640
Everything just burned!

592
00:47:24,680 --> 00:47:25,680
-What?
-What?

593
00:47:27,520 --> 00:47:30,720
After that, we were banned
from camping forever.

594
00:47:31,920 --> 00:47:32,960
Our first trip…

595
00:47:33,280 --> 00:47:34,160
and our last.

596
00:47:35,120 --> 00:47:36,240
The end.

597
00:47:36,440 --> 00:47:38,960
How big was the campsite
for you to get banned?

598
00:47:40,280 --> 00:47:41,320
The whole mountain.

599
00:47:41,600 --> 00:47:42,480
The whole mountain?

600
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:44,120
You guys deserved it.

601
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:47,440
Marn, Mork. Come eat.

602
00:47:53,760 --> 00:47:55,280
Still, I loved it.

603
00:47:55,720 --> 00:47:57,080
The three of us
crammed into one little tent,

604
00:47:57,080 --> 00:47:58,360
doing everything together.

605
00:47:58,400 --> 00:47:59,160
It was fun.

606
00:48:00,360 --> 00:48:03,680
You three have done so much together.

607
00:48:06,080 --> 00:48:07,280
They didn’t have any other friends.

608
00:48:07,680 --> 00:48:09,480
I didn’t exactly have a choice.

609
00:48:12,240 --> 00:48:13,160
-Mok!
-Mok!

610
00:48:26,120 --> 00:48:26,960
Mr. Peach,

611
00:48:27,920 --> 00:48:30,960
Mr. Rome’s departure has been moved up.

612
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:34,560
P’Kian already told me.

613
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:37,760
Come visit us whenever you can.

614
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:47,160
I’ve spent my whole life
as Mr. Thee’s right-hand man.

615
00:48:47,400 --> 00:48:48,920
Now that I’m really leaving…

616
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:52,200
it feels strange.

617
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:56,120
Go live your life, Mr. Mok.

618
00:48:57,760 --> 00:48:58,880
As for P’Kian…

619
00:49:00,480 --> 00:49:01,760
you can leave him to me.

620
00:49:04,080 --> 00:49:06,360
You take good care of Mr. Thee.

621
00:49:08,600 --> 00:49:12,320
I’ve known that ever since
you came into Mr. Thee’s life.

622
00:49:16,040 --> 00:49:17,160
If not you…

623
00:49:17,880 --> 00:49:19,160
I don’t know who else could.

624
00:49:29,960 --> 00:49:31,240
And you and Mr. Rome,

625
00:49:32,600 --> 00:49:34,240
I hope everything works out for you both.

626
00:49:34,840 --> 00:49:36,960
Thank you, Mr. Peach.

627
00:49:44,080 --> 00:49:44,880
Mr. Mok.

628
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:47,080
Yes?

629
00:49:48,920 --> 00:49:50,560
With the schedule moved up,

630
00:49:51,320 --> 00:49:53,280
do we still have a little time left?

631
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:02,040
Ahem.

632
00:50:08,960 --> 00:50:10,960
It’s been a while
since our last honeymoon,

633
00:50:11,880 --> 00:50:14,680
so I thought this would be a good chance.

634
00:50:15,160 --> 00:50:16,360
What’s the occasion?

635
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:20,360
I just wanted to spend time with you.

636
00:50:21,520 --> 00:50:22,240
Isn’t that enough?

637
00:50:26,400 --> 00:50:27,960
It’s a long drive.

638
00:50:29,200 --> 00:50:30,760
I’m getting hungry.

639
00:50:32,640 --> 00:50:33,560
Can I…

640
00:50:34,920 --> 00:50:36,520
have a little something first?

641
00:50:42,880 --> 00:50:44,240
Have a drink for now.

642
00:50:45,600 --> 00:50:48,160
You can have the full course
when we get there.

643
00:50:48,680 --> 00:50:49,360
Exactly!

644
00:50:49,840 --> 00:50:51,040
I’m starving.

645
00:50:53,400 --> 00:50:54,840
I thought you were going back
to Hong Kong.

646
00:50:55,040 --> 00:50:56,760
Don’t just hear
what you want to hear, bro.

647
00:50:57,200 --> 00:51:00,040
I said I’m going back
after Mok has fully recovered.

648
00:51:03,920 --> 00:51:04,560
Uh…

649
00:51:06,280 --> 00:51:06,960
I…

650
00:51:07,840 --> 00:51:09,360
I’m still a little injured, dude, sir.

651
00:51:10,840 --> 00:51:11,760
Ant-bite level.

652
00:51:17,160 --> 00:51:21,480
Lookpeach, this isn’t
my idea of a honeymoon.

653
00:51:22,120 --> 00:51:24,360
The more, the merrier.

654
00:51:27,160 --> 00:51:27,720
Hold on.

655
00:51:32,000 --> 00:51:33,600
We must separate the tents.

656
00:51:33,760 --> 00:51:35,880
One for us, and one for them.

657
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:38,760
And put them far apart.

658
00:51:38,880 --> 00:51:40,720
Far enough that they can’t hear any noise.

659
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:44,960
He means…

660
00:51:45,200 --> 00:51:46,240
I snore.

661
00:51:49,400 --> 00:51:50,160
Whoo!

662
00:51:50,640 --> 00:51:51,400
Smashing.

663
00:51:53,000 --> 00:51:54,200
It’s gonna be smashing.

664
00:52:19,200 --> 00:52:20,080
What are you doing?

665
00:52:20,920 --> 00:52:21,840
Why do you look so serious?

666
00:52:22,160 --> 00:52:23,840
There’s a series script
and a casting call.

667
00:52:23,880 --> 00:52:24,760
A series?

668
00:52:36,640 --> 00:52:37,280
Hey.

669
00:52:38,000 --> 00:52:39,880
I got a casting call too.

670
00:52:45,480 --> 00:52:46,560
It’s the same series.

671
00:52:50,120 --> 00:52:53,120
Aran, don’t you think
the title’s a little strange?

672
00:52:53,400 --> 00:52:54,520
It sounds familiar, yeah?

673
00:53:07,400 --> 00:53:08,680
- Do you like this trip, P’Kian?

674
00:53:08,680 --> 00:53:10,680
- This trip will become a wonderful memory for us.

675
00:53:10,680 --> 00:53:12,920
- Do you want to watch
our story together, Lookpeach?

676
00:53:13,200 --> 00:53:13,840
- I don’t think I can.

677
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:17,000
- Not only are you refusing to row,
but you’re abandoning the ship too.

678
00:53:17,120 --> 00:53:19,480
- I’m not used to seeing you
so close to other people.

679
00:53:19,560 --> 00:53:20,280
- I’m jealous.

680
00:53:20,280 --> 00:53:21,400
- You’re jealous, Lookpeach?!

681
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:23,920
- Was all that astronomy talk
just so you could lead up to your surprise?

682
00:53:23,920 --> 00:53:27,360
- I’d wrap even the entire universe
in a ribbon and give it to you,

683
00:53:27,360 --> 00:53:28,640
- if that’s what you want.

684
00:53:28,760 --> 00:53:32,160
- Just how far is Theerakit Kian Lee willing to go?
